From: HakiOS <hakios@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 0004/4] bsd/sys: fall back to the host SDK's availability.pl

The iPhoneOS SDK does not ship usr/local/libexec at all:

    $ ls $(xcrun -sdk iphoneos -show-sdk-path)/usr/local/libexec
    No such file or directory

bsd/sys/make_symbol_aliasing.sh builds its input path as

    AVAILABILITY_PL="${SDKROOT}/${DRIVERKITROOT}/usr/local/libexec/availability.pl"

so any kernel build with SDKROOT pointing at the iPhoneOS SDK dies at
do_build_setup with:

    Unable to locate .../iPhoneOS26.5.sdk//usr/local/libexec/availability.pl
    make[5]: *** [_symbol_aliasing.h] Error 1

which surfaces three make levels up as "Error 2" in bsd/sys and tells you
nothing about the real cause. It has nothing to do with the target SoC —
a stock XNU build for iPhoneOS hits it too.

availability.pl is the same perl script in every SDK and answers both
--ios and --macosx, so use the host (macOS) SDK copy when the target SDK
has none. If neither exists the original error is kept, so nothing is
hidden.

---
--- a/bsd/sys/make_symbol_aliasing.sh
+++ b/bsd/sys/make_symbol_aliasing.sh
@@ -37,8 +37,22 @@
 AVAILABILITY_PL="${SDKROOT}/${DRIVERKITROOT}/usr/local/libexec/availability.pl"
 
 if [ ! -x "${AVAILABILITY_PL}" ] ; then
-    echo "Unable to locate ${AVAILABILITY_PL} (or not executable)" >&2
-    exit 1
+    #
+    # HakiOS: the iPhoneOS SDK does not ship usr/local/libexec at all, so an
+    # XNU kernel build against SDKROOT=<iPhoneOS.sdk> always dies here with
+    # "Unable to locate ... availability.pl". The script is identical in every
+    # SDK and answers both --ios and --macosx, so fall back to the host
+    # (macOS) SDK copy when the target SDK has none.
+    #
+    HAKIOS_HOST_SDK="$(xcrun --sdk macosx --show-sdk-path 2>/dev/null)"
+    if [ -n "${HAKIOS_HOST_SDK}" ] && \
+       [ -x "${HAKIOS_HOST_SDK}/usr/local/libexec/availability.pl" ] ; then
+        AVAILABILITY_PL="${HAKIOS_HOST_SDK}/usr/local/libexec/availability.pl"
+        echo "note: ${SDKROOT} has no availability.pl; using host SDK copy" >&2
+    else
+        echo "Unable to locate ${AVAILABILITY_PL} (or not executable)" >&2
+        exit 1
+    fi
 fi
 	    
 {
